  "spoken_content": [
    {
      "start_seconds": 0,
      "end_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Without stomach acid, you're in trouble.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 4.9,
      "end_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "You see, you need it to be like battery acid in there.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 8.2,
      "end_seconds": 13.9,
      "text": "Without the battery acid in that pouch. And this bag right here.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 15,
      "end_seconds": 19.2,
      "text": "The food isn't going to get broken down properly.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 20.5,
      "end_seconds": 23,
      "text": "Now you got chunks of food.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 24.3,
      "end_seconds": 27,
      "text": "And it's going to ferment.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 27.9,
      "end_seconds": 30,
      "text": "And guess what happens when it ferments?",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 30,
      "end_seconds": 36.6,
      "text": "It becomes gassy and it starts shooting back up like a volcano.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 37.5,
      "end_seconds": 42,
      "text": "The medical monopoly calls this acid reflux.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 43,
      "end_seconds": 48.8,
      "text": "If it happens chronically all the time, that's called GERD.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 51.3,
      "end_seconds": 57.6,
      "text": "Acid reflux. Not only does it feel uncomfortable,",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 57.6,
      "end_seconds": 67.9,
      "text": "but if you have GERD and it's happening all the time now, you're setting yourself up to have Barrett's esophagus.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 68.9,
      "end_seconds": 73.9,
      "text": "And that's essentially where the esophagus gets all burned up.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 74.9,
      "end_seconds": 78,
      "text": "Some people may even damage their vocal cords.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 78.9,
      "end_seconds": 85,
      "text": "Their voice might even change.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 85,
      "end_seconds": 92,
      "text": "If you've ever met someone very hoarse voice and they're not a smoker,",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 92,
      "end_seconds": 98,
      "text": "they probably don't have enough battery acid in that stomach.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 99,
      "end_seconds": 102,
      "text": "This is your first line of defense.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 105.9,
      "end_seconds": 110,
      "text": "You eat the food, it goes down the pipe.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 110,
      "end_seconds": 114,
      "text": "It goes into a bag of battery acid.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 114,
      "end_seconds": 122,
      "text": "It gets broken down and it slips out in the duodenum into the small intestine and so on and so forth.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 122,
